    Inheritance:
      NXobject/identifierNAME
        Doc       : An identifier for a (persistent) resource. An identifier, provided by some
                    authority, that has been assigned to an object described by this ``NXobject``.
                    To be useful, the identifier must not be reassigned to a different real-world
                    object. It is typical for there to be some mechanism to resolve an identifier,
                    obtaining metadata about the object. Identifiers for which some guarantees exist
                    regarding this resolution process are called persistent identifiers. Persistent
                    identifiers are also known as PIDs.

  GROUP /Su1s/instrument [NXinstrument]  (21 members)
    Concept   : NXxps/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT  [REQUIRED]
    Inheritance:
      NXxps/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT
        Doc       : Description of the XPS spectrometer and its individual parts. This concept is
                    related to term `12.58`_ of the ISO 18115-1:2023 standard. .. _12.58:
                    https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso:18115:-1:ed-3:v1:en:term:12.58
      NXmpes/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT
        Doc       : Description of the photoemission spectrometer and its individual parts. This
                    concept is related to term `12.58`_ of the ISO 18115-1:2023 standard. .. _12.58:
                    https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso:18115:-1:ed-3:v1:en:term:12.58
      NXentry/INSTRUMENT
      NXinstrument
        Doc       : Collection of the components of the instrument or beamline. Template of
                    instrument descriptions comprising various beamline components. Each component
                    will also be a NeXus group defined by its distance from the sample. Negative
                    distances represent beamline components that are before the sample while
                    positive distances represent components that are after the sample. This device
                    allows the unique identification of beamline components in a way that is valid
                    for both reactor and pulsed instrumentation.
    @default = electronanalyzer  [OPTIONAL]

    GROUP /Su1s/instrument/beam_probe [NXbeam]  (4 members)
      Concept   : NXxps/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/beam_probe  [REQUIRED]
      Inheritance:
        NXxps/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/beam_probe
        NXmpes/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/beam_probe
          Doc       : Properties of the probe beam at a given location. This is the beam that is
                      used to facilitate the photoemission during MPES experiments.
        NXinstrument/BEAM
        NXbeam
          Doc       : Properties of the neutron or X-ray beam at a given location. This group is
                      intended to be referenced by beamline component groups within the
                      :ref:`NXinstrument` group or by the :ref:`NXsample` group. This group is
                      especially valuable in storing the results of instrument simulations in which
                      it is useful to specify the beam profile, time distribution etc. at each
                      beamline component. Otherwise, its most likely use is in the :ref:`NXsample`
                      group in which it defines the results of the neutron scattering by the sample,
                      e.g., energy transfer, polarizations. Finally, There are cases where the beam
                      is considered as a beamline component and this group may be defined as a
                      subgroup directly inside :ref:`NXinstrument`, in which case it is recommended
                      that the position of the beam is specified by an :ref:`NXtransformations`
                      group, unless the beam is at the origin (which is the sample). Note that
                      ``incident_wavelength``, ``incident_energy``, and related fields can be a
                      scalar values or arrays, depending on the use case. To support these use
                      cases, the explicit dimensionality of these fields is not specified, but it
                      can be inferred by the presence of and shape of accompanying fields, such as
                      incident_wavelength_weights for a polychromatic beam.
      FIELD /Su1s/instrument/beam_probe/associated_source  shape=()  dtype=object
        Value     : /entry/instrument/source_probe
        Concept   : NXmpes/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/beam_probe/associated_source  [RECOMMENDED]
        Inheritance:
          NXmpes/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/beam_probe/associated_source
            Doc       : The source that emitted this beam. Should be named with the same suffix,
                        e.g., for ``beam_probe`` it should refer to ``source_probe``. This should be
                        specified if an associated source exists. Example: *
                        /entry/instrument/beam_probe/associated_source =
                        /entry/instrument/source_probe
      FIELD /Su1s/instrument/beam_probe/distance  shape=()  dtype=float64
        Value     : 0.0
        Concept   : NXmpes/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/beam_probe/distance  [RECOMMENDED]
        Inheritance:
          NXmpes/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/beam_probe/distance
            Doc       : Distance between the point where the current NXbeam instance is evaluating
                        the beam properties and the point where the beam interacts with the sample.
                        For photoemission, the latter is the point where the the centre of the beam
                        touches the sample surface.
          NXbeam/distance
            Doc       : Distance from sample. Note, it is recommended to use NXtransformations
                        instead.
        @units = mm  [UNIT: NX_LENGTH]
      FIELD /Su1s/instrument/beam_probe/extent  shape=()  dtype=float64
        Value     : 200.0
        Concept   : NXmpes/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/beam_probe/extent  [RECOMMENDED]
        Dims      : nP × 2
        Inheritance:
          NXmpes/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/beam_probe/extent
          NXbeam/extent
            Doc       : Size of the beam entering this component. Note this represents a rectangular
                        beam aperture, and values represent FWHM. If applicable, the first dimension
                        shall represent the extent in the direction parallel to the azimuthal
                        reference plane (by default it is [1,0,0]), and the second dimension shall
                        be the normal to the reference plane (by default it is [0,1,0]).
        @units = um  [UNIT: NX_LENGTH]
      FIELD /Su1s/instrument/beam_probe/incident_energy  shape=()  dtype=float64
        Value     : 1486.6
        Concept   : NXmpes/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/beam_probe/incident_energy  [REQUIRED]
        Dims      : m
        Inheritance:
          NXmpes/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/beam_probe/incident_energy
          NXbeam/incident_energy
            Doc       : Energy carried by each particle of the beam on entering the given location.
                        Several use cases are permitted, depending on the presence or absence of
                        other ``incident_energy_X`` fields. The usage should follow that of
                        :ref:`incident_wavelength </NXbeam/incident_wavelength-field>`.
        @units = eV  [UNIT: NX_ENERGY]
